> Recently, I've been thinking a bit about the power of two-weaponing,
> and how it tends to destroy some variety with combat classes.  One
> possible balancing idea that I came up with would be to disallow
> two-weapon combat with any artifacts.  This would make shields useful
> again, as they would become more attractive to combat classes that
> want to wield artifacts.  It'd also make the Tsurugi more interesting,
> as it isn't quite so overshadowed by the other possibilities.
> Finally, I think it'd give people a somewhat more difficult choice to
> make, choosing between the power granted by two-weaponing, or the
> ability to use an artifact weapon.

My first thought was that you were talking about slash-em, where you're
able to twoweapon with 2 artifacts.  But if I've read you correctly,
you're actually suggesting the opposite -- that artifacts should not just
refuse to be held second, but should refuse to be held at all with another
weapon.  Is that correct?

I like it.  It'd balance the overpowered effects of twoweaponing a little
bit... twoweapon with longswords would be a little better than Frost Brand
or Grayswandir, but at the expense of a shield.  It would also take more
scrolls.

Another thought I had was that, when twoweaponing, your secondary weapon
should have to be small -- say, a knife or dagger.  I imagine this would
make silver daggers very popular, though...



